mintcare (1.12.18) noble; urgency=medium

  * Processes: new Find memory wasters button. It lists your own programs
    that have been idle for 30 minutes or more while holding 200 MB or more
    of memory, and older idle copies of a program that is running twice.
    The desktop session, MintCare and other users' processes are never
    listed. Ticked programs are asked to close; any that don't close are
    offered a force end.

 -- Matthew Allwood <matthewallwood@protonmail.com>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:46:31 +0000

mintcare (1.12.17) noble; urgency=medium

  * Timeshift file restore: restored files are owned by root and lose the
    snapshot's setuid and setgid bits. Files with file capabilities are
    refused. Symlinks in the snapshot are skipped, and a destination path
    that goes through a symlink is refused.
  * Timeshift file restore now needs a trusted backup drive. Use Trust this
    drive on the Timeshift snapshots tab once; restores from a drive with
    another serial number are refused.
  * Malware quarantine: files move through folder handles, never replace a
    file already in the quarantine folder, and are refused when on another
    disk. File names that are not UTF-8 are matched and shown safely.
  * Failed SSH logins are counted only from sshd's own services.
  * Clearing execute bits leaves top-level symlinks alone.
  * Tests no longer need a real home folder, so Launchpad builds pass.

 -- Matthew Allwood <matthewallwood@protonmail.com>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 10:56:16 +0000

