mintcare (1.12.14) noble; urgency=medium

  * Backup: when some files can't be read, the backup keeps what it copied
    and reports how many files it skipped. A failed backup no longer leaves a
    partial copy behind.
  * Backup: the size estimate leaves out the folders and files that the
    exclude list skips.
  * Downloads: new downloads are checked one at a time, so unpacking many
    files at once no longer starts a scan for each of them.
  * Clean: the stale cache clean keeps pip, yarn, go-build and Hugging Face
    caches. Scheduled cleaning runs only its safe items, whatever the
    settings file says.
  * Clean: each item removes exactly the folders its scan listed.
  * Firewall: turning the firewall on keeps SSH open when an SSH server is
    running, so remote login still works.
  * Optimise: the I/O scheduler revert puts back each disk's previous
    scheduler.
  * Processes: details for an open process load in the background, and the
    package lookup is kept for each program.
  * Timers, the tray entry and the restart work when MintCare's path contains
    spaces.
  * Reports and the support bundle mask IP and MAC addresses.
  * Updates: a download bigger than the release says is refused.

