mintcare (1.12.13) noble; urgency=medium

  * Security: disk encryption and auditd checks, and a read-only Lynis
    hardening audit card.
  * Security: connections right now per program, and devices on your network
    with new ones flagged.
  * Security: real-time protection with decoy files and ClamAV checks of
    downloads, both optional.
  * Security: updates install only when their checksums carry a valid
    signature from the MintCare release key.
  * Hardware: short and long SMART self-test buttons; error counters are
    tracked over time and warn when they grow.
  * Processes: lower the priority of your own programs; Restore priority asks
    for your password.
  * Maintenance: threshold alerts every 15 minutes for a full disk, a low
    battery, or a hot processor or drive.
  * Boot errors: dismiss the ones you have looked at; dismissals last until
    the next boot.
  * Flatpak: the update count refreshes on Rescan and after an update.
  * Failed-login reader: the cost is bounded per line, so a very long journal
    line cannot slow the check.

